  Non-deficiency (<s>anyūnatā</s>). The completeness of categories, without remainder — this is called non-deficiency. The categories are: ten supplementary topics (<s>cūlikārthas</s>) and fifty dispositions (<s>pratyayas</s>). Among these, existence and oneness are established by the five 'existent [topics].' Purposefulness is the cause-effect relationship. Subservience to another (<s>pārārthya</s>) — because composite things serve another's purpose. Hence also otherness [from <s>Puruṣa</s>]. From the <s>guṇa</s>-triad (<s>guṇatraya</s>), from the power of consciousness, from birth, death, and the instruments, etc. — the plurality of <s>Puruṣas</s>. 'For the sake of the seeing of <s>Puruṣa</s>' — conjunction. 'When bodily separation is reached' — separation. 'From the attainment of correct knowledge' — residual activity. 'And from that [comes] the reversal' — the non-agency of <s>Puruṣa</s>. These are the ten supplementary topics.
