  From what? — it is said: True, that is so. Nevertheless, doubt arises. From what? Because when one instrument grasps its own object, eagerness of another instrument is observed. Here, when an object such as the form of a mango, pomegranate, and the like is perceived by one instrument — the eye — the eagerness and operation of another instrument — characterized as the tongue — is observed. If the <s>indriyas</s> are restricted to their own objects, then upon perceiving another instrument's object, there should not be a state of grasping one's own object through the expectation of companionship with that [other instrument]. But there is. Therefore the doubt is justified. What, then, is your understanding on this matter?
  [Reply:] Here too there is no overlap in the grasping of their own objects by the <s>indriyas</s>. Rather:

